{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"The `search` service was down, and it's running again. I submitted the mitigation once with an empty solution, and the endpoint accepted it.\n\n**Cause:** the namespace has a `ResourceQuota` called `memory-limit-quota` (`memory: 1Gi`). It requires every pod to set a memory limit. The `search` deployment set only CPU limits and requests, so its pods were rejected with `must specify memory for: hotel-reserv-search`. The `search` service had no endpoints, so requests that depend on it failed.\n\n**Fix:** I ran `kubectl set resources deploy/search -n hotel-reservation --limits=memory=512Mi --requests=memory=256Mi`. The new pod started, registered with consul, and the rollout completed. Before submitting, I checked that no pod was in a non-Running state.\n\n**Left as is:** I did not delete the quota. The other pods have no memory limits, so they would also be rejected if they were ever recreated. They are unaffected for now, since the quota only checks pods when they are created.\n\nI didn't run any end-to-end requests against the frontend to confirm latency."}}
